Residue: `ls internal/handlers/explorer/ | grep zz_probe` -> nothing; the post-run
`git status --porcelain` above is unchanged from the pre-run one. The EXIT trap fired.

On the repaired probe's soundness (advisory; my verdict is on the implementation):
the three documented repairs are all real and correctly made — storage.New's two-value
return, the identical-content fixtures that exact-hash dedup would collapse (Hash is
sha256(date|lower(desc)|amount)[:8] with no file/account component — I re-read
transaction.go:67-75 and confirm), and the dropped dl.Transactions() pin (LoadData already
returns *models.TransactionSet). One residual weakness I would not have let stand:
TestProbeA2_CreditKindForcesSignFlip's assertion is a `for ... if tx.Amount > 0 { fail }`
loop, which passes vacuously if the loader returned zero rows. Check 8 makes total
starvation unlikely and the repo's own tests assert exact row counts, so this does not
change the outcome — but the probe is weaker than the worker's test on exactly the axis
the oracle exists to police.

