loader.go:230-237 — `func (dl *DataLoader) UnassignedCount() int`, as pinned.

models.Transaction: I diffed the added/removed lines mechanically rather than eyeballing.
The ONLY semantic addition is `AccountID string \`json:"account_id,omitempty"\``; the other
+/- pairs are pure gofmt re-alignment of the existing ID/Date/Amount and
Category/TransactionType/SourceFile/Hash tag columns (identical text, different padding).
No StableID, TransferPairKey, or TransferClass. ComputeHash (transaction.go:67-75) is
untouched and does NOT include AccountID, so adding the field cannot perturb any existing
transaction identity.

